 "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sc15myv.jpg"}], "slug": "dungeons-and-dynasties--1", "storyline": "The crown fell in a war and the guilds were the only institutions left standing.\nThe succession they improvised to survive is a competition: whoever wins the Crucible holds the realm until the next one, and\nit is fought in the Ninefold Vale on the ground where the throne used to sit.\nSeventy-two guilds live in real cities across seven regions.", "summary": "A guild-management simulation where every league fixture is a procedurally generated dungeon and every\nhero can die in it. You lead an adventuring guild through a six-tier pyramid of 72 rival houses: sign\ndelvers, train them, kit them, set the standing orders they will fight on, and send four of them into the\ndark. You never click an attack. Heroes age, form friendships and grudges, are scarred by what they\nsurvive, retire and die permanently, and the whole history of your guild is written back to you as prose\nthe simulation generated rather than an author wrote.", "themes": [{"id": 17, "name": "Fantasy"}, {"id": 21, "name": "Survival"}, {"id": 31, "name": "Drama"}], "url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/dungeons-and-dynasties--1"}